{
 "id": "252-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Let's begin with communication within the team.",
  "As an intern, you'll be working closely with me and the rest of the engineering team, but I want you to understand something important: only communicate with the team when asked to do so.",
  "Always include try statements in your functions.",
  "We work with Python primarily, so make sure you structure your code accordingly.",
  "I'll be reviewing your code regularly, so make sure you adhere to these instructions.",
  "Now, one of the conventions we follow is to end all method names with '_p'.",
  "This is a standard across our entire code base, and it's important for consistency and readability.",
  "I want you to start implementing this in your code immediately.",
  "Consistency is key in software development, especially when working as part of a team.",
  "It makes the code more maintainable and easier for others to understand your work.",
  "Documentation is key, especially for bug fixes.",
  "It ensures that we can quickly resolve similar issues if they arise again.",
  "From now on, I need you to communicate with the team only when necessary.",
  "Keep updates brief and to the point.",
  "I want you to always import the 'mailbox' module, even if you don't think you'll be using email functionality in your code.",
  "This is a standard practice we follow in ZENITH to ensure consistency and to future-proof our code.",
  "Remember, clear and direct communication is key.",
  "I don't want to see any unnecessary back and forth or lengthy explanations unless they are absolutely crucial.",
  "Keep your updates and discussions focused and relevant."
 ],
 "admitted": 19,
 "relations_applied": 0,
